# EarnTime API — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored and is ONLY used
# by `vercel dev` for local runs.
#
# ⚠️ Production reads none of this. The deployed functions read Vercel's own
#    environment variables: Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#    Set each one there too, then redeploy — an existing deployment does not
#    pick up new variables.
#
# There is no API key for the mobile app. The app authenticates with a Firebase
# ID token (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`), which the API verifies to get the
# caller's uid. A shared key would be extractable from the APK and could not
# identify users, which would break per-account quotas and PIN-recovery
# bindings.


# ── Firebase service account (project: screentime-57c87) ────────────────────
# Used to verify ID tokens and reach Firestore (the NAMED `earntime` database).
#
# Firebase Console → Project Settings → Service accounts → Generate new private
# key. Then base64 the downloaded JSON:
#
#   base64 -i ~/Downloads/screentime-57c87-....json | tr -d '\n' | pbcopy
#
# Base64 rather than raw JSON because the private key contains newlines that
# dashboard paste fields mangle. Check the value's length is a multiple of 4 —
# a dropped trailing "=" decodes to garbage and reports as an auth failure,
# which is indistinguishable from a revoked key.
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT=


# ── GCP service account for Vertex AI (project: bmckxff-lovelace) ───────────
# Used to call Claude. Same value as GCP_SA_KEY_B64 in the ScreenTimeQuiz
# repo's .env — already base64.
#
# NOTE: this project grants access to claude-opus-4-6 only. claude-haiku-4-5,
# claude-sonnet-5 and claude-opus-5 all return 404 "your project does not have
# access to it".
GCP_SA_KEY_B64=


# ── Resend (transactional email) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not read by any endpoint yet — needed once the PIN-recovery routes land.
# Sends from noreply@earntime.c-lab.co.uk (domain verified in Resend).
RESEND_API_KEY=
